From 39da60da77877fa7fa656631cae05d8edb7d834c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:19:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Bluetooth: keep SCO when the driver writes the voice
 setting itself

hci_cc_read_buffer_size() disables SCO (sco_pkts = 0) when the voice
setting cannot be read, since commit 14d17c78a4b1 ("Bluetooth: Disable
SCO support if READ_VOICE_SETTING is unsupported/broken"): a SCO
connection without the proper voice setting can lock the controller up.

The voice setting can also be made known the other way round: a driver
whose controller answers HCI_OP_READ_VOICE_SETTING wrongly but accepts
HCI_OP_WRITE_VOICE_SETTING can write it once the controller is
initialized (after its HCI_Reset), in its post_init callback, before any
SCO connection can be made. hci_cc_write_voice_setting() then stores it
in hdev->voice_setting and notifies the driver, and btusb picks the
isochronous alternate setting from it.

Add HCI_QUIRK_VOICE_SETTING_BY_DRIVER for such a driver: the SCO buffers
the controller reports are kept. The driver disables SCO itself when its
write fails. Nothing changes for a controller without the quirk, also
with HCI_QUIRK_FIXUP_BUFFER_SIZE set (force_scofix).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 include/net/bluetooth/hci.h | 11 +++++++++++
 net/bluetooth/hci_event.c   |  7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h b/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h
index 1641d879d..7d04e1cc4 100644
--- a/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h
+++ b/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h
@@ -375,6 +375,17 @@ enum {
 	 */
 	HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_READ_PAGE_SCAN_TYPE,
 
+	/* When this quirk is set, the driver writes the voice setting
+	 * (HCI_OP_WRITE_VOICE_SETTING) itself in its post_init callback,
+	 * so SCO stays enabled with the buffer sizes the controller
+	 * reports even though HCI_OP_READ_VOICE_SETTING cannot be used.
+	 * If that write fails, the driver disables SCO (sco_pkts = 0).
+	 *
+	 * This quirk can be set before hci_register_dev is called or
+	 * during the hdev->setup vendor callback.
+	 */
+	HCI_QUIRK_VOICE_SETTING_BY_DRIVER,
+
 	__HCI_NUM_QUIRKS,
 };
 
diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
index 03b805207..d5eea0d41 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
@@ -947,7 +947,12 @@ static u8 hci_cc_read_buffer_size(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data,
 		hdev->sco_pkts = 8;
 	}
 
-	if (!read_voice_setting_capable(hdev))
+	/* A SCO connection without the proper voice setting can lock the
+	 * controller up, so SCO is disabled when the voice setting cannot
+	 * be read, unless the driver writes it itself.
+	 */
+	if (!read_voice_setting_capable(hdev) &&
+	    !hci_test_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_VOICE_SETTING_BY_DRIVER))
 		hdev->sco_pkts = 0;
 
 	hdev->acl_cnt = hdev->acl_pkts;
